    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There are only three test files (`AcceptanceTest`, its abstract base `AcceptanceBase`, and one other non-`@Test` helper), and all 2 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response (an `OwnerDto`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field plus getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` and a `membershipTier(Owner)` default method following the existing `membershipNumber`/`displayName` pattern:\n   - Returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present.\n   - Returns `\"BRONZE\"` otherwise (including null/absent email, or any positive namesake count).\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass:\n- `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` \u2014 unique owner (namesakeCount 0) with email \u2192 `SILVER`.\n- `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` \u2014 owner with no email \u2192 `BRONZE`.",
